1. CHARGE PUMP — CP Mirror Pairs
--------------------------------------------------------------------
Block: sky130_cp (cp_pmos_array.mag + cp_nmos_array.mag)
Matched pairs per circuit note (sky130-fr001 fix):

PMOS pair M_pbias / M_psrc:
  Sizes:       W=4um, L=2um, nf=4 (both identical)
  Strategy:    6-finger interdigitated array
  Arrangement: [Dum_P][M_pbias][M_psrc][M_psrc][M_pbias][Dum_P]
  N-well:      Single shared nwell island (96x24 lambda = 48x12 um)
  Dummy devices: 2 edge dummies (left and right) to equalise litho env
  Source tie:  All PMOS sources → common VDD rail (li1 horizontal)
  Gate-drain:  M_pbias diode-connected (D=G=pbias via poly-to-li short)
  Pbias net:   B-finger drains connected by horizontal li1 at y=4l
  Psrc_g net:  S-finger drains by li1 at y=8l
  Symmetry:    Common-centroid: each pbias finger sees identical
               neighbour context (psrc on both sides)
  Expected post-layout mismatch: < 1% (systematic gradient cancelled)
  Pre-layout sim mismatch: 0.37% (sky130-fr001 fix applied)

NMOS pair M_nbias / M_nsrc:
  Sizes:       W=1.5um, L=2um, nf=1 (both identical)
  Strategy:    4-finger interdigitated array
  Arrangement: [Dum_N][M_nbias][M_nsrc][Dum_N]
  P-substrate: ndiff in p-sub, no nwell needed
  Dummy devices: 2 edge dummies
  Source tie:  All NMOS sources → VSS rail
  Gate-drain:  M_nbias diode-connected
  Symmetry:    Common-centroid with dummies
  Expected post-layout mismatch: < 1%

Additional CP devices (non-matched, less critical):
  M_psw (PMOS switch, W=8u L=150n nf=8): placed in CP region,
        not in matched array — switch Ron << bias mirror R
  M_nsw (NMOS switch, W=4u L=150n nf=4): similar
  M_pinv_p/n (switch inverter): standard CMOS inverter placement
  Rbias_p=90k, Rbias_n=91k: serpentine poly resistors in CP region
  → NOTE: Rbias_p/Rbias_n layout not yet detailed (stubbed in this
    iteration). These are single-use resistors (not matched pairs)
    so common-centroid is not required; poly serpentine to be added
    in routing refinement pass.

2. RING VCO — Stage Symmetry
--------------------------------------------------------------------
Block: sky130_vco_layout.mag (5 × vco_stage_unit.mag)
Stages: 5 identical inverter stages with current-starved tails

Stage unit cell (vco_stage_unit):
  PMOS load:  W=2u L=150n nf=2 (pdiff in nwell)
  NMOS driver:W=1u L=150n nf=1 (ndiff in p-sub)
  CS tail:    W=1u L=2u nf=1 (long-gate NMOS for current starving)
  Layout:     Vertical stack: CS(bot) → NMOS(mid) → PMOS(top)
  Symmetry:   All 5 stages placed in identical unit cells at equal
              x-pitch (12 lambda = 6 um) → matched parasitics
  Ring nodes: Horizontal li1 ring (n1→n2→...→n5→n1)
  Vtune bus:  met1 horizontal rail at y=3l connecting all CS gates
  Output buf: Same unit cell scaled, placed at stage 6 position

VCO matching assessment:
  - All stages have identical geometry (no inter-stage mismatch)
  - Vtune gate capacitance per stage: equal (shared gate line)
  - Stage parasitics symmetric by construction
  - Ring closure (n5→n1) uses met2 bypass over stages (slight
    asymmetry at stage 5 → monitor in post-layout sim)

3. BIAS GENERATOR — PMOS Mirror
--------------------------------------------------------------------
Block: sky130_bias_layout.mag

PMOS reference pair M_p1 / M_p2 / M_p_out:
  M_p1:  W=1u L=2u (reference)
  M_p2:  W=2u L=2u (1:2 ratio → 2× current)
  Arrangement: [M_p1][M_p2][M_p2'][M_p1'][M_p_out]
  Strategy: M_p2 split into 2 equal fingers interleaved with M_p1
  Matching: 1:2 current ratio maintained by geometry
  nwell: single common island

NMOS pair M_n1 / M_n2:
  W=2u L=2u both → 1:1 mirror
  Placed adjacently in p-sub
  Degeneration resistor Rd=1.8k under M_n1 source

