6. AREA SUMMARY
--------------------------------------------------------------------
Target total area: 50,000 um2
Actual top-level bbox: 336×196 = 65,856 um2 (OVER BUDGET by 32%)

Root cause of area overage:
  LF capacitor array (C1 predominantly): 117×80 um = 9,360 um2
  plus LF R2/R3 serpentine region: ~30×50 um = 1,500 um2
  LF total footprint in top-level placement: ~150×95 um = 14,250 um2

  Top-level placement also includes:
  - Guard rings (4 lambda = 2 um each side): adds ~15 um perimeter
  - Routing channels between blocks: ~20-30 um
  - Top-level power ring: 8 lambda = 4 um each side

  The architecture budgeted area_um2=15,000 for LF which is correct;
  the top-level assembly floorplan did not pack blocks tightly enough
  (vertical stack of BIAS+PFD at full height adds unused whitespace).

  TO CLOSE AREA TO 50,000 um2:
  1. Pack BIAS (40×30 um real) + CP arrays more tightly → save ~800 um2
  2. Use smaller C1 cap cells (cap_vpp_04p4x04p6 × many more) for denser fill
  3. Compact the PFD/FBDIV/POSTDIV stub cells (they are oversized estimates)
  4. Remove guard ring whitespace; integrate well taps into block rows

